{"id":"sermeq-kujalleq","name":"Sermeq Kujalleq (Jakobshavn), Greenland","region":"Greenland","continent":"Arctic","change_type":"glacier","product":"GOFF","bbox":[-50.4,69.05,-48.8,69.3],"story":{"headline":"One of the world's fastest glaciers, tracked every 12 days","what":"Ice surface speed from pixel offset tracking between repeat passes: the fast trunk runs at roughly 17-28 m/day through the season, the surrounding ice at 2-4 m/day.","physics":"Phase interferometry fails on fast-flowing, melting ice (coherence is lost), so features are cross-correlated between images; L-band penetrates the snow surface and keeps texture through melt season.","drivers":"Warm Atlantic water melting the floating tongue, summer melt lubricating the bed, seasonal ice-melange buttressing.","caveats":"Offsets over 12 days near the calving front can exceed the search window; check the SNR layer. A single pair can under-read speed when surface melt destroys the texture being tracked - treat an isolated dip as tracking loss, not a slowdown."},"window":["2026-06-17","2026-11-10"],"bounds":[-50.4,69.05,-48.8,69.3],"center":[-49.599999999999994,69.175],"demo":false,"band":"L","layers":{"frames":{"kind":"sequential","items":[{"date":"2026-07-05","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20260705.webp"},{"date":"2026-07-17","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20260717.webp"},{"date":"2026-08-10","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20260810.webp"},{"date":"2026-08-22","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20260822.webp"},{"date":"2026-09-03","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20260903.webp"},{"date":"2026-09-15","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20260915.webp"},{"date":"2026-09-27","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20260927.webp"},{"date":"2026-10-09","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20261009.webp"},{"date":"2026-10-21","url":"sites/sermeq-kujalleq/frames/20261021.webp"}],"title":"Ice surface speed","legend":{"type":"sequential","vmin":0,"vmax":33.0,"unit":"m/day","ramp":["#cde2fb","#6da7ec","